ctly ; thus they have agreed to forward a full payment history and amortization schedule. Our concerns are the misapplication of payments intended for reduction of principal balance, deceptive practices by BAC as they did not previously nor beforehand explain their policy in applying overage payments of our mortgage towards future payments, BAC ignored written instructions on each payment they received from us to apply overage payments to the principal balance, and BAC 's inappropriate practices proactively worked to inhibit the early payoff of our mortgage loan. We are filing a formal complaint against Bank of America and their inappropriate practices that work to inhibit early payoffs for mortgage loans. We also want to issue a formal complaint that Bank of America proactively worked against our original mortgage agreement that explains no penalty for early payoff.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION",PA,18901,,Web,2023-08-22,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
